00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:56.293
and also rural spaces as well,
especially along the border.

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.560
I was particularly interested in this,

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:03.280
this historical episode called La Matanza,

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:06.930
which was basically a period
of state sanction violence

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:11.620
in the late 1800s, early
1900s against Mexicans,

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:16.520
and Mexican Americans,
the Texas State Rangers,

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:21.003
for instance, carried on this
long campaign of murdering,

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:27.100
Mexicans that they either
charged with fictitious crimes

00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:32.100
or simply killed out of
spite or out of hate.

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:37.263
And it tore families apart,

00:23:38.370 --> 00:23:42.910
really did a lot to
undermine the influence

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:45.959
and the power of Mexicans who
had established themselves

00:23:45.959 --> 00:23:47.267
in the lower Rio Grande Valley

00:23:47.267 --> 00:23:50.070
and other places along the border.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:52.720
So I've been thinking about that and then

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:57.250
thinking also about the
fact of migration as well

00:23:57.250 --> 00:24:02.250
and how we as a nation treat
those who are either refugees

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.000
or migrants moving across
the border to the US

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:12.790
from other places, whether it's Mexico

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:15.370
or Latin America or wherever.

00:24:15.370 --> 00:24:19.050
